1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,640
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,397
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:29,600
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:30,060 --> 00:00:35,260
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:40,460
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,680
One Piece.

15
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:52,557
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:58,477
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:03,897
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

18
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,117
Is only legendary till
someone proves it real?

19
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:14,437
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times!

20
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

21
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,077
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

22
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:24,277
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

23
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:30,560
So come aboard and bring along
All your hopes and dreams.

24
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:35,960
Together we will find everything
That we're looking for?

25
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,697
There's always room for you!

26
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:42,420
If you wanna be my friend.

27
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:46,860
We are, we are on a cruise!

28
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,720
We are

29
00:01:51,340 --> 00:01:53,040
Oh, so hungry.

30
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:56,157
When the hell are we going
to reach land, anyway?

31
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,070
Who knows?

32
00:01:57,360 --> 00:02:01,536
We're just sailing on the wind and
the waves, going where they take us.

33
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:04,057
Don't you find it dumb that
someone trying to be king

34
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:06,997
of the pirates doesn't have
a single navigational skill?

35
00:02:07,080 --> 00:02:07,960
Not really.

36
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,520
I just drift around.

37
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,080
What about you?

38
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:13,977
Aren't you some famous bounty
hunter who sailed the seas?

39
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:18,119
I don't have any recollection of
ever calling myself a bounty hunter.

40
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:22,320
I set out onto the open sea
in search of just one man,

41
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:24,957
but then I couldn't
get back to my village.

42
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:28,757
By that point, I had no choice but to
go after pirate ships to earn a living.

43
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:29,670
Oh, I see.

44
00:02:29,753 --> 00:02:30,837
So you're just lost.

45
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,567
Hey, don't let it like that!

46
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:40,860
Heh heh, another big haul today.

47
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,137
That's two in a row.

48
00:02:42,220 --> 00:02:45,337
All of this should keep Buggy
from getting too mad at us.

49
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:47,596
Hey, what's with that boat out there?

50
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:53,220
We should check it out.

51
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,460
Oh, it's a lady.

52
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:11,240
Hey, wake up, little girl.

53
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,671
Please tell me i'm not dreaming this time?

54
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:19,845
Finding help out here in
the middle of nowhere.

55
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,677
If you're real, then please.

56
00:03:21,760 --> 00:03:23,407
Could you get me some water?

57
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:24,740
I'm so thirsty.

58
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,517
I'll give you as much jewelry
and valuables as you like!

59
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,517
If you could just give
me one little drink?

60
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,177
No sweat, we'll help you.

61
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:35,797
But not until we see what kind
of treasure you're holding on to.

62
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:38,820
Yeah, don't mind us, we'll just be a man.

63
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,797
I can't get the damn thing open.

64
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,700
Okay, hold up, here we go.

65
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:52,311
If you want, you can keep the whole thing.

66
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,620
It's not my style.

67
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:55,980
But that's our boat!

68
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:57,500
You tricked us!

69
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:01,277
From the look of those clouds
moving in from the south,

70
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:03,125
I'd say a cold front's coming.

71
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:07,894
So you can probably expect strong
winds and squalls any time now, really.

72
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,059
Also, in that small boat, and you
run a bit of a chance of capsizing.

73
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:22,130
Bingo!

74
00:04:23,400 --> 00:04:24,240
See ya!

75
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:27,840
I'll just take whatever
treasure you guys got here!

76
00:04:27,940 --> 00:04:29,800
Get back here, you bitch!

77
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,374
I'll get you for this!

78
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:34,180
Ugh, I am so hungry.

79
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,340
It's killing me.

80
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:42,000
Hey, look, a bird. I
know! Let's eat it! Huh?

81
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,340
How do we catch it?

82
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:44,500
Leave that to me!

83
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,560
GUM-GUM-PROCKET!

84
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:51,480
Makes sense.

85
00:05:01,080 --> 00:05:02,440
You moron!

86
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,266
What the hell's going on now?

87
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:10,390
Hey!

88
00:05:10,473 --> 00:05:11,303
You there!

89
00:05:11,386 --> 00:05:12,216
Stop!

90
00:05:12,299 --> 00:05:13,129
Please!

91
00:05:13,212 --> 00:05:14,042
Man overboard!

92
00:05:14,125 --> 00:05:14,955
Stop!

93
00:05:15,038 --> 00:05:15,868
Man overboard!

94
00:05:15,951 --> 00:05:16,781
I can't believe I find
shipwreckers at a time like this!

95
00:05:16,864 --> 00:05:17,700
I can't stop!

96
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:19,840
You're just gonna have to jump in!

97
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,190
What?!

98
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,437
I'm actually impressed
you made it on board!

99
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:26,897
Are you trying to kill us?!

100
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:28,720
Stop the boat now!

101
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:32,837
The three of us are members of
Back the Clown's pirate crew!

102
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:34,500
This boat is ours now!

103
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:36,170
Huh?

104
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:42,582
I'm sorry, we had no idea you were
the famous pirate hunter Zoro.

105
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,720
Please forgive us.

106
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:48,336
Thanks to you three idiots,
I lost sight of my friend.

107
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,920
So just keep paddling. Yes, sir.

108
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:55,460
Knowing Luffy, he'll probably pull
off something once he spots land.

109
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:59,900
So, any ideas about what we do now?

110
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:01,337
Good question.

111
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:06,400
If Captain Buggy finds out a girl stole
our boat and our treasure, we're history.

112
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:08,080
I know. Huh?

113
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:09,931
So who is this Buggy guy?

114
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:12,735
You've never heard of Buggy the Clown?

115
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,110
Nope.

116
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:17,247
He's the ruthless captain
of our pirate ship.

117
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:19,457
And he's eaten one of the devil fruits.

118
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:23,620
But above everything else, he
is one truly terrifying man.

119
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:44,377
Yes I finally got it.

120
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:45,877
Hey girl, get back here!

121
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:50,617
You better give us that map back or else
we just stole that chart of the Grand Line.

122
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,137
It belongs to us!

123
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:53,557
Damn it!

124
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:55,637
If we don't get that
thing back then we're...

125
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,737
You're as good as dead.

126
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:59,879
We'll be killed by one of
the captain's cannonballs!

127
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,500
Captain Buggy!

128
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:07,660
I spotted something high
in the sky above the pond!

129
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:09,420
Well, shoot it down!

130
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:16,980
What's that?

131
00:07:27,080 --> 00:07:28,560
What was that?

132
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:29,940
What the hell?

133
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,200
A guy fell from the sky.

134
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:36,140
Dammit, why were there
cannonballs flying at me?

135
00:07:40,920 --> 00:07:42,740
At least I'm safe now.

136
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:46,340
And what just happened to me was awesome.

137
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:52,217
Geez, I'm so hungry.

138
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:55,420
Oh, hey boss, thanks for
coming to save me. Huh?

139
00:07:56,800 --> 00:07:57,700
Who are you?

140
00:07:59,880 --> 00:08:02,260
They're all yours now, boss! Have fun!

141
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:07,165
Hey, that girl's getting away!

142
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:09,277
That's okay, we've got her boss now.

143
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,740
You're in trouble, kid.

144
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:13,537
You should've let your
crony fit for herself.

145
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:16,177
You guys know of anywhere
good to eat around here?

146
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:18,436
Food's the least of your worries now!

147
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:31,037
You better keep your hands
off my hat you bastard

148
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,900
i wonder if they've
killed that poor guy yet

149
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,920
wow you're really strong

150
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:53,777
even though both of them had sabers
you beat them barehanded Hey,

151
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:55,217
you're the girl who set me up.

152
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,130
Who are you?

153
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:59,397
I'm a talented thief who
steals strictly from pirates.

154
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,421
The name's Nami.

155
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:02,366
Hey, want to team up with me?

156
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:05,745
Um, thanks anyway, lady,
but I think I'll pass.

157
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:07,640
Hold on!

158
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,165
At least think about it first!

159
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:16,637
You're telling me they still
haven't caught the thief?

160
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:19,277
Uh, not yet, but...

161
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,125
But they should be in pursuit.

162
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,732
Right now, Captain, sir.

163
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:28,117
Now explain to me, how in the world did
she manage to get her hands on that chart?

164
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,030
Huh?

165
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:34,160
If we're preparing to enter the
Grand Line and go on a rampage,

166
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,177
then why wasn't the
chart properly guarded?

167
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:37,217
I don't know, sir.

168
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:40,817
The map was just sitting out,
plain as the nose on your face.

169
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:41,960
What did you say?

170
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:44,937
I mean, it was easy for
her to find and take it.

171
00:09:45,020 --> 00:09:47,196
Did you hear something about my nose?

172
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:51,437
Sir, are you trying to tell
me you find my nose funny?

173
00:09:51,520 --> 00:09:53,420
Is my nose amusing?

174
00:09:53,880 --> 00:09:55,409
No sir, you misunderstood!

175
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:57,960
Oh no, you were quite clear!

176
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:02,350
Help me!

177
00:10:07,860 --> 00:10:09,160
This isn't good!

178
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:11,720
He's gonna use the Devil Fruit power!

179
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,780
Tell me, who am I?

180
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:23,810
Captain...

181
00:10:23,893 --> 00:10:30,540
And what happens if someone defies me?

182
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:32,230
Flashy...

183
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:34,430
Death...

184
00:10:35,840 --> 00:10:36,670
Await...

185
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,010
Them...

186
00:10:38,093 --> 00:10:38,923
Please...

187
00:10:40,420 --> 00:10:41,700
Forgive me...

188
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,800
Quit your groveling.

189
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:48,078
I'll overlook your slip-up
and forgive you this time.

190
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:50,497
But you better get that chart back.

191
00:10:50,580 --> 00:10:53,160
Don't screw up again, or else.

192
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:55,320
Yes, Captain Buggy!

193
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:02,130
Yum.

194
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:05,017
So, do you live in this
big house all by yourself?

195
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:06,177
This isn't my house.

196
00:11:06,260 --> 00:11:08,317
I'm just staying here for the time being.

197
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:10,997
Everyone's left this town
because of Captain Buggy.

198
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:13,700
So you're just a petty thief. How rude.

199
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,900
I only steal from people
who deserve it. Pirates.

200
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:20,180
So don't compare me to
some scumbag petty thief.

201
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:23,388
The thief's a thief as
far as I'm concerned.

202
00:11:24,120 --> 00:11:26,557
My goal is to earn a
hundred million berries,

203
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:29,346
no matter how hard it
is or how long it takes.

204
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,457
What do you need so
many berries for anyway?

205
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:33,500
It's a secret.

206
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:36,135
But with this chart of the Grand Line,

207
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:39,301
the hundred million is now
a definite possibility.

208
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,070
A chart?

209
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:42,980
So you must be a navigator.

210
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:46,732
I'm the most skilled navigator
you're ever likely to meet.

211
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:48,777
Oh wow, that's perfect!

212
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:50,717
Then how about you join my crew?

213
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,617
I've been looking to recruit a navigator.

214
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:53,880
Really? Sure.

215
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:56,160
You can be our newest crew member.

216
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:57,390
No.

217
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:01,940
I suppose this means
you're a pirate. Yeah.

218
00:12:02,180 --> 00:12:03,620
I made a solemn promise.

219
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:05,697
I promised the guy who
gave me this hat that I'd

220
00:12:05,780 --> 00:12:08,604
form a crew and become
the greatest pirate ever.

221
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:12,237
There's nothing in this world
that I despise more than pirates.

222
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:14,940
I only like money and tangerines. Come on.

223
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,980
Be our navigator. I said no.

224
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,110
You're lost.

225
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:22,571
Did you find her or what?

226
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:24,505
No, I can't find her anywhere.

227
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,017
Where could she be hiding?

228
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:30,317
I don't know, but we're going to be in big
trouble if we don't get that chart back.

229
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:32,341
I got to do something about them.

230
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:36,197
I guess I might consider joining you,

231
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,657
but only if you'll agree
to certain conditions.

232
00:12:38,740 --> 00:12:39,570
Really?

233
00:12:39,653 --> 00:12:40,483
I'll do anything.

234
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:44,397
Well, then I want you to come with me to
pay a little visit to Buggy the Pirate.

235
00:12:44,480 --> 00:12:45,340
But first...

236
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,637
Why did you have to tie me up?

237
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:52,602
The rope's just for appearances.

238
00:12:53,200 --> 00:12:54,340
Well, okay, then.

239
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:57,697
I've been looking forward to meeting
some other pirates, so let's get going.

240
00:12:57,780 --> 00:12:58,877
Just hold your horses.

241
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,136
What's the big rush?

242
00:13:00,480 --> 00:13:01,310
What?

243
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:04,975
Are you telling me the thief got away?

244
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:08,540
Please forgive us, Captain Buggy.

245
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:11,777
I've never seen a more
pathetic group than you three.

246
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:12,860
Time to die!

247
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,300
Captain Buggy, I have news!

248
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:17,640
What is it?

249
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,557
The girl who stole our chart is back.

250
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:20,617
And with a prisoner.

251
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:21,530
What?

252
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:24,510
It's her!

253
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:27,368
That's the sneaky thief
who stole the chart!

254
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:35,137
I've captured the thief,
Captain Buggy the Clown.

255
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:36,808
And here's your chart back.

256
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:42,126
Not that I don't appreciate it, but why
the sudden change of heart, little girl?

257
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:48,517
I had another fight with my boss,
and I just can't take it anymore.

258
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:51,365
So I thought I'd see if
I could join your crew.

259
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,120
You're fed up, huh?

260
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:02,317
I must admit you're an amusing girl.

261
00:14:02,400 --> 00:14:03,230
I like you.

262
00:14:03,320 --> 00:14:05,144
Of course you can join my crew.

263
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,737
I've successfully infiltrated them.

264
00:14:11,820 --> 00:14:14,349
Pirates are so dumb
and easy to manipulate.

265
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:17,700
Hey, guys, why am I in a cage?

266
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:22,300
It's a great day to be a pilot.

267
00:14:22,740 --> 00:14:25,480
Girl, what do you call yourself? I'm Nami.

268
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:30,037
Then let's have a welcome
party for our new friend Nami.

269
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,061
Let's celebrate!

270
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,010
What's wrong?

271
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:53,180
We're throwing this party
in your honor, so eat up!

272
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,278
Thanks for the party, Captain Buggy.

273
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:00,997
I'll just keep my eyes peeled for
a chance to take back that chart.

274
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:04,786
Maybe I'll swipe all of Buggy's
treasure, too, while I'm at it.

275
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,480
Ah! Damn it!

276
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:19,340
This is such a flashy party.

277
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:21,200
Now listen up!

278
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:25,120
Men, it's time to prepare the buggy ball!

279
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:44,180
All set, Captain.

280
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,460
What are you doing with that thing?

281
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:51,620
Just observe the awesome might
of the buggy ball. Light it.

282
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:15,120
That was one heck of an explosion.

283
00:16:15,300 --> 00:16:19,006
It looked like it was one of the
captain's beloved buggy balls.

284
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:20,220
Buggy balls?

285
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:34,080
That was flashy.

286
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:36,697
With these buggy balls
and my Devil Fruit powers,

287
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:39,677
I should have no problem
conquering the Grand Line.

288
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:43,480
Right, Nami? Right! Yes, of course! Huh?

289
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,080
But it's my destiny to
conquer the Grand Line!

290
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:52,666
And then I'm gonna become
King of the Pirates!

291
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:54,000
Shut up, idiot!

292
00:16:57,260 --> 00:17:00,780
I can see why you're sick
of him, Nami! Yeah, I know.

293
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:04,457
He never takes anything seriously,
thinks that life's a big game.

294
00:17:04,540 --> 00:17:06,069
He acts like a little kid!

295
00:17:07,820 --> 00:17:08,650
I see.

296
00:17:08,733 --> 00:17:12,840
Then how about I give you a buggy
ball to blow away your old boss?

297
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:19,797
It'll be a great opportunity for you to
prove your loyalty to me, your new captain.

298
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:20,710
Men?

299
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:29,697
That's alright, Captain.

300
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:31,477
We don't have to finish him off quite yet.

301
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:35,148
Let's get back to the welcoming
party and just have more fun.

302
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:38,900
This is my idea of having more fun!

303
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:49,380
If I don't shoot, I'll be killed.

304
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:54,140
But if I do shoot, then I'm
no better than these pirates.

305
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:59,509
Fire!

306
00:17:59,592 --> 00:18:00,422
Now!

307
00:18:00,505 --> 00:18:01,335
Light the fuse, Nami!

308
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,134
You're not whipping out on me, are you?

309
00:18:15,280 --> 00:18:16,677
FIRE! FIRE! FIRE!

310
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:17,819
What's the matter?

311
00:18:18,040 --> 00:18:19,393
Your hands are shaking.

312
00:18:20,420 --> 00:18:21,377
FIRE! FIRE!

313
00:18:21,460 --> 00:18:24,937
That's what happens when you take
on pirates with half-ass resolve.

314
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,420
FIRE! FIRE! Resolve? To do what?

315
00:18:27,700 --> 00:18:29,700
To kill someone like it's nothing?

316
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:32,120
Is that a pirate's resolve? No.

317
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,840
FIRE! FIRE! FIRE!

318
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:38,785
You've got to be willing
to risk your own life.

319
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:45,180
Here, new chick.

320
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:46,832
Quit being such a tease.

321
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,393
Let me show you how to light the cannon.

322
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:01,240
My mistake! Sorry!

323
00:19:02,660 --> 00:19:03,490
Nami!

324
00:19:03,573 --> 00:19:05,559
What's the meaning of this outrage?

325
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:06,850
I'm sorry.

326
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:08,010
What's wrong?

327
00:19:08,093 --> 00:19:09,413
Just shoot him already!

328
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:10,930
Huh.

329
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:13,657
So, now you've decided to save me?

330
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:14,860
Don't be so stupid!

331
00:19:15,220 --> 00:19:17,157
I'm not doing this for you, you idiot!

332
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:20,897
I just don't want to lower myself to
the level of these inhuman pirates!

333
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:22,560
Okay, thanks anyway.

334
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:25,617
Pirates took the life of
a person very dear to me.

335
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:27,229
I'll never be one of them!

336
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:28,580
Oh, I see.

337
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,200
Nabi, the fuse!

338
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:37,371
So you think pirates are just
inhuman filth, is that right?

339
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:38,440
Get her, man!

340
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:51,460
Water, water, water, water, water.

341
00:19:56,560 --> 00:19:57,520
Not good.

342
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:05,710
Whoa!

343
00:20:11,380 --> 00:20:12,240
Watch out!

344
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:21,780
Hey, now.

345
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:26,040
It's not very nice of you guns
to gang up on a poor girl.

346
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:28,750
Zoro!

347
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:35,750
You hurt?

348
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,100
I said, are you hurt?

349
00:20:40,120 --> 00:20:41,600
No, I'm fine, I think.

350
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:44,140
Phew, what a relief.

351
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:45,874
I'm glad you found us.

352
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:48,037
Now hurry up and come get me out of here.

353
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,257
How do you keep getting
yourself into these situations?

354
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:53,717
First a bird flies off with you, and
now I find you trapped in a cage.

355
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,918
It's an interesting story, actually.

356
00:20:56,960 --> 00:21:00,019
That's, yeah, that little
brat just called him Zoro.

357
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:05,180
The crew he mentioned earlier
was the pirate hunter Zoro?

358
00:21:06,280 --> 00:21:07,780
What's going on here?

359
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:10,320
So you're Zoro.

360
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:15,221
If you're here for my head, you've
got quite a struggle before you.

361
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:17,340
No, not interested.

362
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:19,180
I gave up pirate hunting.

363
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:20,773
I'm here for my friend.

364
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,180
But I'm interested, though.

365
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:26,012
Killing you would boast to my reputation.

366
00:21:26,320 --> 00:21:28,660
If you try, you'll die.

367
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:35,960
I tried to warn you, but oh well

368
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:16,540
That wasn't much of a
fight, now was it? Oh, wow!

369
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,000
He's weak!

370
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:20,160
Way to go, Zoro! No way!

371
00:22:30,820 --> 00:22:32,420
Hey, why are they laughing?

372
00:22:32,740 --> 00:22:36,277
Their captain is lying dead on the
ground and yet they're still laughing?

373
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:37,320
What's going on?

374
00:22:37,660 --> 00:22:40,480
Fellas, what do you find so damn funny?

375
00:22:49,060 --> 00:22:49,890
Zoro!

376
00:22:51,560 --> 00:22:52,880
Bucky's still alive!

377
00:22:53,180 --> 00:22:54,160
What the hell?

378
00:22:58,820 --> 00:23:00,500
The chop-chop fruit.

379
00:23:01,900 --> 00:23:05,488
That's the name of the devil
fruit that's given me my powers.

380
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:10,380
I'm a chop-chop person, and now I
can never be defeated by the sword!

381
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:15,660
His limbs re-attach?

382
00:23:15,840 --> 00:23:19,437
And I always thought that the devil fruits
were just a story that pirates told.

383
00:23:19,520 --> 00:23:21,280
So he's a chop-chop man?

384
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,635
That's pretty freaky.

385
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:29,437
I didn't hit any vital organs, but
that's a serious wound you have there,

386
00:23:29,520 --> 00:23:32,800
so I'm guessing that I am the winner!

387
00:23:38,140 --> 00:23:39,217
Oh, crap!

388
00:23:39,300 --> 00:23:40,660
The tables have turned!

389
00:23:40,940 --> 00:23:44,881
If we don't do something quick,
they're gonna kill all three of us!

390
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:47,460
I let my guard down.

391
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:48,620
Stupid mistake.

392
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:58,057
Buggy! Buggy! Buggy!

393
00:23:58,140 --> 00:24:01,720
Stabbing him in the back was
a cowardly move, you big nose!

394
00:24:06,160 --> 00:24:06,990
You idiot!

395
00:24:07,073 --> 00:24:07,903
Don't call him that!

396
00:24:07,986 --> 00:24:09,038
What are you doing?

397
00:24:12,280 --> 00:24:13,180
What's that?

398
00:24:13,540 --> 00:24:15,420
You said?

399
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:17,780
I got a big nose!

400
00:24:19,060 --> 00:24:19,890
Luffy!

401
00:24:21,920 --> 00:24:22,750
Buggy!

402
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:27,395
I'M GONNA KICK YOUR ASS SOON
AS I GET OUT OF THIS CAGE!

403
00:24:31,640 --> 00:24:33,280
YOU KICK MY ASS?

404
00:24:33,400 --> 00:24:35,137
YOU 'VE GOT A LOT OF NERVE, KID!

405
00:24:35,220 --> 00:24:38,197
NOW I'M AFRAID ALL THREE OF YOU
ARE GOING TO DIE HERE TODAY!

406
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:39,820
BY MY OWN HAND!

407
00:24:40,220 --> 00:24:43,985
SO IF YOU'RE GOING TO DO ANY ASS
KICKING, YOU BETTER DO IT SOON!

408
00:24:47,380 --> 00:24:49,660
WE'RE DONE FOR, IT'S ALL OVER!

409
00:24:53,360 --> 00:24:55,300
I refuse to die!

410
00:24:55,860 --> 00:24:57,700
Zoro, get up! What?

411
00:24:58,340 --> 00:25:01,477
You better have a really good
plan or else we're all dead!

412
00:25:01,560 --> 00:25:03,325
So what are you guys gonna do?

413
00:25:08,820 --> 00:25:09,920
I got you.

414
00:25:10,500 --> 00:25:12,260
Nothing makes sense anymore.

415
00:25:12,680 --> 00:25:14,500
This is why I hate pirates!

416
00:25:15,300 --> 00:25:16,160
You're a fool!

417
00:25:16,880 --> 00:25:18,080
Time to die!

418
00:25:25,520 --> 00:25:30,080
Your three-sword style has no effect
on me, I already told you. I ne...

419
00:25:31,140 --> 00:25:31,970
Hey!

420
00:25:32,053 --> 00:25:33,704
Listen what I'm talking to you!

421
00:25:49,680 --> 00:25:50,880
No! Crap!

422
00:25:51,040 --> 00:25:52,900
The cannon's pointed at us! No!

423
00:25:53,620 --> 00:25:54,720
Hurry! Light it!

424
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:59,320
Huh? Do it now! Right! Wait! Just wait!

425
00:25:59,700 --> 00:26:02,297
The cannon's still loaded
with a special buckyball!

426
00:26:02,380 --> 00:26:04,017
I don't wanna go out like this!

427
00:26:04,100 --> 00:26:05,520
Shut in by my own balls!

428
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:10,147
I can't believe you just did
that, you ungrateful little girl!

429
00:26:10,580 --> 00:26:12,320
Wait! No! Stop!

430
00:26:12,740 --> 00:26:13,800
Stop it now!

431
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:30,920
You okay, Zoro?

432
00:26:31,120 --> 00:26:32,532
How bad are you injured?

433
00:26:32,720 --> 00:26:35,057
Just shut up and don't
worry about how I'm doing.

434
00:26:35,140 --> 00:26:38,493
I need to concentrate if I'm
going to get us out of this.

435
00:26:43,040 --> 00:26:44,960
Who is this guy?

436
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:49,400
Hey, Luffy. Who's this?

437
00:26:49,660 --> 00:26:51,480
Who's the girl? Oh, right.

438
00:26:51,680 --> 00:26:53,092
She's our new navigator.

439
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:55,960
I'm not so sure about that.

440
00:26:56,220 --> 00:26:57,691
Who are you guys, anyway?

441
00:26:58,860 --> 00:26:59,690
Move.

442
00:27:01,100 --> 00:27:02,200
You're in the way.

443
00:27:14,960 --> 00:27:18,480
I guess even a lowly pirate
can still rescue his friend.

444
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:30,117
As a kid, I never stopped.

445
00:27:30,200 --> 00:27:32,697
Searching for a great treasure!

446
00:27:32,780 --> 00:27:37,457
I had a map in my mind.

447
00:27:37,540 --> 00:27:40,097
That I knew would lead me.

448
00:27:40,180 --> 00:27:44,297
I had to find my way to that place!

449
00:27:44,380 --> 00:27:47,197
Before someone could beat me.

450
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:53,720
The promised land was in my
grasp, and I wouldn't let go!

451
00:28:02,280 --> 00:28:07,260
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true!

452
00:28:09,220 --> 00:28:15,657
But if the world ever
changes, I call out your name!

453
00:28:15,740 --> 00:28:22,657
We return to the time when
everything's the same.

454
00:28:22,740 --> 00:28:29,537
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

455
00:28:29,620 --> 00:28:34,700
Waiting for that one true dream?
